  "prefLabel": "Rev 1602.02 Disaggregated Charges",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 1602.02 Disaggregated Charges.\n\n(a) Services provided by a retailer to a customer shall not be included in the gross charge when:\n\n(1) They are not necessary for, or directly related, to the provision of communications services;\n\n(2) They are identified as separate services to the customer; and\n\n(3) The cost for such services are disaggregated.\n\n(b) Disaggregated services shall include, but not be limited to the following:\n\n(1) Directory advertising;\n\n(2) Consulting services;\n\n(3) Billing and collection revenue; and\n\n(4) Non-communication products.\n\nSource. #4799, Interim, eff 8-22-90, exp. 6-1-90; ss by #4954, eff 10-16-90; ss by #6336, eff 9-24-96; ss by #8178, eff 9-24-04; ss by #10213, eff 10-24-12; ss by #13553, eff 2-7-23 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Rev 1600)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev1600.html"
